&lt;p data-start=&quot;3808&quot; data-end=&quot;3831&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity &amp;amp; Inclusion&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is deeply important to us. Through our ally network, we support under-represented groups and&amp;nbsp;maintain&amp;nbsp;a working environment free from bias, harassment, or discrimination. We encourage candidates from all backgrounds to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re also happy to make adjustments to the hiring process to ensure every candidate can participate fully.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note:&lt;/strong&gt; Netcraft does not accept unsolicited approaches from external recruiters.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/netcraft/backend-engineering-team-lead-london-manchester-386369","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"London, Manchester","created_at":1793526913},{"slug":"senior-platform-engineer-london-260230","company_name":"V7Labs.com","title":"Senior Platform Engineer","description":"<h2><strong>V7</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At V7, we’re building AI platforms that help humans do their best work, at incredible scale and speed. Our mission is to turn human knowledge into trustworthy AI, making complex tasks faster, smarter, and more accurate.  We’re growing fast, backed by leading investors and AI pioneers (including the minds behind Transformers and Gemini).  <br /></p><h2><br /><strong>The product</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">V7 Go helps teams turn complex, repeatable work into AI workflows they can run, review and improve<strong>.</strong> Built for private markets, insurance and real estate, it supports investment diligence, underwriting, claims review and portfolio reporting—from analysing documents and data to generating deliverables and updating connected systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your experts define how the work should be done. V7 combines reusable Skills, shared company knowledge and configurable workflows, with citations, audit logs and human review to help teams verify results and control key decisions. It supports models including GPT, Claude and Gemini.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build workflows around your processes.</strong> Configure each stage, choose models and tools, and set review steps where human judgement matters. Teams can inspect sources, correct outputs and refine workflows over time. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.v7labs.com/tables">Explore workflows</a>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Give every workflow your firm’s knowledge.</strong> The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.v7labs.com/context-graph">Context Graph</a> connects documents, entities, relationships and source evidence, creating institutional memory that teams and agents can draw on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn analysis into work your team can use.</strong> Generate editable memos, reports, presentations and spreadsheets, and connect workflows to the tools your business already uses. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.v7labs.com/slides">Explore document generation</a>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The team you’ll be joining and impact you’ll have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A small Platform team with a very wide remit: cloud, SRE, DevOps, developer experience, compliance, and the infrastructure behind our AI products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We run AWS first across multiple regions, with GCP and Azure alongside. Our model providers come through all three, so this is genuinely multi-cloud work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're in the process of making everything faster, more reliable and nicer to work with, for enterprise customers who expect a lot. There are a number of compliance and big expansion projects on the horizon</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our engineers lean heavily on AI coding agents and sandboxes. You’ll shape how that works across the company, giving people freedom while keeping us in control.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What you’ll be doing from day one:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owning our infrastructure as code in Terraform, plus alerting, observability (Prometheus, Grafana) and reliability, including load testing and disaster recovery exercises.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Making CI/CD faster (GitHub Actions, ArgoCD) and taking obstacles out of engineers’ way, from build times to how they run AI agents day to day.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Running the platform behind our AI workloads across Bedrock, Vertex AI and Azure, with a close eye on reliability and cost.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Getting on calls with enterprise customers and our commercial team to troubleshoot and answer infrastructure and security questions. Alongside that, compliance work and a spot on the on-call rotation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong AWS in production, ideally multi-region. Hands-on with GCP, with Azure a bonus. You understand how model consumption works through each cloud.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep experience with Terraform, observability and CI/CD, and you write solid Python (Elixir is a bonus, or you’re keen to learn).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clear communicator who’s happy explaining technical things to a customer, not just to other engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Independent and comfortable with ambiguity. You find problems without being handed tickets, and you don’t mind when priorities flip from one week to the next.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">V7 champions equality and inclusion because diverse teams build better products. Don't check every box? Apply anyway — we value what makes you unique and will support you through the process, just let our Talent team know how they can help.</p><hr><p>Compensation: £100K – £125K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • £100K – £125K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/v7labscom/senior-platform-engineer-london-260230","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793526016},{"slug":"senior-people-partner-content-london-149702","company_name":"9Fin","title":"Senior People Partner - Content","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About 9fin</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">9fin is the AI platform powering global debt markets — the world’s largest asset class at over $145 trillion.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Debt markets are vast, global, and mission-critical, yet still run on fragmented data, PDFs, and manual workflows. 9fin replaces this broken infrastructure with a single platform that centralises proprietary credit data, deep analysis, and high-value workflows across global markets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, 9fin powers teams at 300+ blue-chip institutions worldwide, including global banks, asset managers, private equity firms, law firms, and advisors. The business is scaling at exceptional speed, with rapid expansion in the US and best-in-class retention driven by deep workflow adoption.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re at a defining inflection point. With proven product-market fit and strong, global market pull, 9fin is accelerating toward becoming the category-defining platform for debt markets worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The opportunity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our People Partners are the eyes and ears of the organisation, embedded within their functional areas to be a sounding board for leaders, support managers and enable teams to thrive. The People Partnering team operate on a strategic and tactical level, ensuring the people elements are in place for teams to effectively deliver their strategic objectives (think org design, upskilling, succession planning) whilst also offering one on one support, both structured and ad hoc, to those who need it most.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring an experienced, driven Senior People Partner to partner with our Chief Content Officer and the Content (Editorial, Legals, Credit, Distressed) team. Content is scaling fast across the UK and US, and we need a Senior People Partner who can move at pace, get to grips with what the team actually does, and hold their own with senior editorial and analytical leaders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be fully embedded in the Content team, with a real voice in leadership meetings, editorial rituals and off-sites. You'll know the leads, managers and rising talent well enough to catch the people issues long before they show up in engagement scores or exit interviews.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every day is different, but here's an example of the kind of things you'll work on:</p><h2><strong>Strategic</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Trusted advisor to your leaders</strong>: You'll be the first person Content leadership calls on anything people-related: the confidant, sounding board and thought partner they think alongside, not the person they update after the fact. That kind of trust is earned over time, through showing up and being willing to have the harder conversation when it matters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Right hand person to the CCO:</strong> You know how he thinks about content and his organisation, and are confident acting as his proxy with his leaders to get them to where they need to be.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Locked in on what the team is trying to achieve</strong>: You know Content's goals, what its leaders and teams do. You bring solutions, not just observations, and follow them through to completion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fully embedded in your team</strong>: You're in the rituals, Slack channels and meetings that matter, so you've got a real read on how the team actually works. You cut through the noise to name the actual issue and get it resolved quickly and respectfully.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Catching things early</strong>: You join the dots across 1:1s, skips, engagement data and your own observations to surface people risks while they're still small and easy to fix. You coach leaders and managers to build the same instinct.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Org design</strong>: You advise on org shape, spot gaps and flag future risk areas. You make sure the right people are doing the right jobs at the right level as Content scales across regions and coverage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Talent management</strong>: You know who the key talent is and you work with leaders to develop, stretch and reward them. You support leaders to identify their successors and build the development plans that get them ready. You work proactively with the Talent team on the pipelines for roles you can already see coming.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; development</strong>: You spot where Content teams need to grow — editorial craft, analytical rigour, management skill, leadership development — and you lead the training that plugs the gap. A big part of that is upskilling managers to handle people issues themselves, early and well, rather than escalating them to the CCO. You diagnose early, source or build the right thing, and hold a bar for what impact should look like once it's landed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reward</strong>: You use solid data to inform our salary bands and keep compensation fair across the team, with D&amp;I front of mind. You coach leaders and managers through promotion and salary reviews so decisions are thoughtful, equitable and defensible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Performance</strong>: You help leaders and managers get the best out of their teams, surfacing blockers, coaching through them, and making sure feedback and training actually land. You hold a high bar yourself and help leaders hold one too.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands up for the bigger stuff</strong>: You take on projects that improve the People function as a whole, not just your patch. You scope them properly, influence stakeholders, manage the risks and dependencies, and ship on time.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Tactical</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Employee Relations (ER)</strong>: Following UK employment law, navigating all employee relations within your business area, including but not limited to: managing Performance Improvement Plans (PIPs), resolving claims and grievances in line with policy, probation management, maternity and paternity cases, flexible working requests, conflict management and mediation, and any other employee-to-employee issue that comes up, both formally and informally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Embedding people products</strong>: Working with the wider Partnering team to embed our people products and systems, delivering training, championing adoption and being the go-to person for questions. Delivering product feedback to the wider team on a regular basis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data</strong>: Pulling and analysing the right data to help managers and leaders make good calls  and adding the context that turns numbers into something your leaders can actually use.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Wellbeing support</strong>: 1:1 support to employees when they need it, and making sure they know what mental and physical health support is on offer. Supporting managers through those conversations too.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cultural ambassador</strong>: Working with leaders and managers to reinforce the right behaviours in teams. Being a role model yourself for our values and ways of working, especially as the London office grows.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>About You</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role will be a great fit if you:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take real accountability for pushing back on leaders — not just flagging a concern and moving on, but staying with it until the right decision gets made.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Can confidently challenge executives and their most senior leaders when it matters, as a true partner rather than a service function.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are properly curious about the business you support. You'll want to understand how Content produces its analysis, what makes a great desk, and what separates a good journalist from a world class one. You ask questions until you get to the real answer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are a strong influencer, able to help others look at things from different perspectives and understand the 'why' behind decisions. Comfortable pushing back on leaders and managers when needed, and know when to step back and let them make their own call.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have significant experience partnering with content, editorial, research or analyst teams and can speak their language credibly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have a bias to action: you see what needs doing and pick it up, rather than waiting to be asked.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use data to back your decisions and see what's coming, not just to describe what's already happened.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Care about data integrity and have solid experience with the day-to-day people processes and onboarding a high-trust team relies on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have a strong grasp of UK employment law and awareness of New York employment law to reach the right, compliant call in tricky ER situations autonomously. Sharp on policies and procedures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Can context-switch frequently and comfortably hold strategic and tactical work in the same day.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are a strong team player who partners closely with your fellow People Partners, Talent Partners and the wider People and Talent team so 9finners get the best experience of us collectively.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Can operate autonomously and at pace in a fast-moving scale-up.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Requirements:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience in HR, preferably in fast-paced environments (tech, fintech, or start-ups)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of UK employment laws and regulations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent organisational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with HRIS and ATS software (we use HiBob, Lattice and Ashby)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional written and verbal communication skills; ability to interact with candidates, employees, and external stakeholders in a professional and approachable manner</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A people-first mindset with the ability to build strong relationships and offer guidance to employees at all levels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible and able to thrive in a fast-moving, dynamic start-up environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactive and collaborative approach</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A genuine interest in employee well-being and fostering a supportive, inclusive culture</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compensation &amp; Benefits</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Finance &amp; Insurance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive base salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity options</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension with 9fin contributing 3% (employee contributions are uncapped)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private health insurance with dental and vision</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time Off</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 vacation days per year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Local public holidays (with option to exchange for alternative days)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work abroad for up to 3 months per year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1-month paid sabbatical after 5 years of service</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhanced parental leave and flexible working arrangements</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth &amp; Culture</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional learning and development budget</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bi-annual team socials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Summer and Winter company-wide events</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hybrid Policy</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">9fin is a hybrid company, and the office is a regular part of how we work. From January 2027, all employees will work from their designated 9fin office on Tuesdays and Wednesdays. Some teams may be asked to be in the office more often, where the nature of their work calls for it. For the rest of the week, you may work from wherever works best for you and your team. Your Talent Partner will share hybrid working details for this role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>9fin is an equal opportunities employer</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At 9fin we are dedicated to building and promoting a fair and inclusive workplace where everyone can reach their full potential and truly belong. We recognize that building diverse teams enables a more creative and productive environment. If you’re excited about this role but your experience doesn’t perfectly align with the job description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You might just be who we’re looking for — either for this role, or perhaps another.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/9fin/senior-people-partner-content-london-149702","tags":["People"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793526014},{"slug":"senior-legal-operations-manager-london-404411","company_name":"9Fin","title":"Senior Legal Operations Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About 9fin</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">9fin is the AI platform powering global debt markets — the world’s largest asset class at over $145 trillion.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Debt markets are vast, global, and mission-critical, yet still run on fragmented data, PDFs, and manual workflows. 9fin replaces this broken infrastructure with a single platform that centralises proprietary credit data, deep analysis, and high-value workflows across global markets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, 9fin powers teams at 300+ blue-chip institutions worldwide, including global banks, asset managers, private equity firms, law firms, and advisors. The business is scaling at exceptional speed, with rapid expansion in the US and best-in-class retention driven by deep workflow adoption.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re at a defining inflection point. With proven product-market fit and strong, global market pull, 9fin is accelerating toward becoming the category-defining platform for debt markets worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The opportunity</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring our first dedicated legal operations team member to sit at the heart of 9fin's growing Legal Affairs function. This is a broad, hands-on role and a rare opportunity to shape how a scale-up in-house legal team runs from the inside out.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own the operational engine of the team: our contract lifecycle platform (Ironclad, which is deeply embedded across sales, procurement and RevOps), our commercial playbook (and developing non-commercial playbooks), our tech stack (including AI implementation), our front-door (right now, ticketing is done in Linear), our knowledge management (currently spread across multiple systems), our reporting and KPIs, and the tracking and governance around outside counsel spend.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll also be a project manager and a hands-on partner to the General Counsel. That includes co-drafting monthly and quarterly business reviews, leading and coordinating cross-functional initiatives  (for example M&amp;A diligence coordination, trademark portfolio work, or regulatory readiness workstreams), and holding a high bar for organisation so nothing on a small, fast-moving team drops.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll report to the General Counsel and work alongside legal colleagues in London and New York. This is a London-based role and we typically expect the team to be in the office three days a week.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you’ll work on</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Below is the shape of the role, laid out as prioritised by Now, Next and Later so you can see the broad strokes of the path ahead - but by no means is this set in stone. Priorities will move as we learn what's most useful in practice and you’ll have a big hand in shaping this further.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Now</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tune legal intake - help us build out the “front door” for legal requests across the business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Sales, Finance, InfoSec and Procurement to streamline deal-desk and approval processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support on knowledge management and internal policy administration. Consolidate knowledge, templates, and other information in a clean accessible structure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build our external legal spend tracker from scratch. Categorise spend, log invoices and quotes, match to matter, and produce a monthly view for the General Counsel.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own KPI reporting improvements against our Ironclad-fed dashboards. Expand coverage into intake, spend, cycle times, and other operational metrics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own operational and reporting support across the Legal function, including responses to internal stakeholders including Finance, RevOps, and the People team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Next</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Get inside and own our tech stack and know it end-to-end - Ironclad, Linear, Google Workspace, Notion, and the AI tools we've adopted or are evaluating.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build, maintain and roll out templates, playbooks and self-serve legal resources so the business can move quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own Ironclad workflow hygiene and adoption end-to-end. Work with the team to clean up metadata and archiving, tighten approvals and signatory workflows, and work with commercial counsel to roll out training across sales, procurement, RevOps and other frequent users.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring structure and visibility across the team. Keep track of open projects, drive follow-through, and make sure balls do not drop across a small team with a lot of surface area.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain our sales contract playbook. Keep it current, propose updates as commercial patterns and RevOps feedback surface them, and make sure the team is actually using it.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Later</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the General Counsel to produce meaningful Exec-level reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist with management of large legal projects on GC instruction. Recent examples include M&amp;A diligence coordination, and trademark portfolio work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support company secretarial administration.</p></li></ul><h2>About you</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a highly organised operator who is energised by building order out of scale-up complexity. You do not need to be a lawyer, but you do need to have run legal operations end-to-end before. The essentials come first below, followed by preferred experience and the traits we care about most.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Highly organised with a systems mindset: </strong>You keep the plates spinning and notice when one wobbles. You see the workflow behind the task and design for repeatability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial, action-biased, comfortable with ambiguity: </strong>You understand what the business needs from legal, get things over the line without waiting to be asked twice, and you're comfortable being the first hire writing the map as you go.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ironclad or equivalent CLM: </strong>Hands-on experience with Ironclad or a directly comparable enterprise CLM (for example Juro, LinkSquares,  Icertis, Agiloft, Leah). We are deeply embedded in Ironclad and you will own it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Legal operations track record: </strong>At least five years' experience running legal operations, contracts operations or a closely adjacent function (compliance operations, legal project management, or legal chief-of-staff), ideally in a scale-up or in-house legal team that is fast paced and where you can demonstrate ownership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>End-to-end project delivery: </strong>You have owned legal or cross-functional projects on your own steam, including timelines, risks, stakeholders and outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reporting and data fluency: </strong>You can build clean dashboards, work with a KPI framework, and translate metrics into a story someone can act on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Outside counsel spend or panel exposure:</strong> Experience setting up spend tracking, panel management or legal project management would be useful, but we're also open to someone with the capability and appetite to build this from scratch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Builder mentality: </strong>Experience as a team’s first or only legal-ops hire, or a member of a small team in the early stage of the build-out of a legal ops function, would be a strong advantage.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a scaling start up, and we enjoy sharing our success, when the company succeeds, we always reinvest that in our people. We also offer huge amounts of responsibility, an abundance of opportunity for growth and a platform to truly excel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Financial &amp; Insurance</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Salary (our salary bands are benchmarked at the top end of the market)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension (your minimum contributions are 4% with 9fin matching up to 7%)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private Medical Insurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid sick leave with Income Protection for long periods of illness</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Group Life Assurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Season Ticket Loan &amp; Cycle to Work schemes</p></li></