<p>As Senior Vet, you’ll lead by example by blending clinical expertise with mentorship and collaboration. You’ll set the tone for quality care, lead in emergency situations, and support the development of your fellow clinicians. You'll have responsibility for:</p>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>* Driving and upholding clinical standards across the clinic</div>
<div>* Supporting the growth, training and wellbeing of your veterinary team</div>
<div>* Identifying clinical development opportunities and shaping team progression</div>
<div>* Championing innovation and service improvement within the clinic</div>
<div>* This is more than a job. This is a vital leadership role with real impact where your guidance helps shape the future of ECC, while making a difference to patients, clients, and colleagues every day.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<h2>Work-Life Balance That Works for You</h2>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<p>This full-time role averages 40 hours per week, including:</p>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>* Nightshifts 1830-0900, Saturday dayshift 1200-1930 and Sunday dayshift 0830-1930</div>
<div>* 1:2 weekends (mix of nights and days)</div>
<div>* No more than three consecutive nights</div>
<div>* Shared bank holidays</div>
<div>* Protected time for leadership duties and meetings</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<p>We understand that life outside of work matters too. That’s why we offer flexibility and can explore part-time arrangements, depending on clinic requirements because your balance is our priority.</p>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<h2>Rewarding Work, Your Way</h2>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<p>We look after you, so you can look after them, by offering a highly competitive salary and a comprehensive benefits package, including:</p>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>* Seven weeks’ pro rata annual leave</div>
<div>* £1,875 CPD allowance + 35 paid CPD hours (pro rata)</div>
<div>* RCVS fees, VECCS membership, and VDS cover</div>
<div>* Private medical insurance</div>
<div>* Family-friendly policies - enhanced maternity, paternity &amp; adoption pay</div>
<div>* Leadership Development Programme</div>
<div>* Access to our AdvantEdge clinical training platform</div>
<div>* Standard pension contributions (5% employee / 3% employer)</div>
<div>* Up to 50% discounted pet care</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<h2>Collaborative Spirit</h2>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<p>You’re never alone at Vets Now: on-shift you’ll work alongside a registered vet nurse, an animal care assistant and a receptionist, and you can contact any of our clinics or referral centers across the UK at anytime, day or night, if needing to discuss a particular case or share ideas.</p>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<p>You’ll also be supported by our Support Office in Dunfermline, where our teams work behind the scenes to help you thrive. Our Call Handlers and Customer Care Advisors ensure you can focus on what matters most - your patients.</p>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
