&lt;p&gt;We look forward to your application!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/xdesign/principal-engineer-contract-352567","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1793505321},{"slug":"patent-engineer-life-sciences-london-142371","company_name":"Ankar","title":"Patent Engineer (Life Sciences)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The way companies innovate is broken.</strong> The systems built to create and protect ideas can’t keep up with the pace of change. Today, <strong>90% of S&amp;P 500 company value is intangible (e.g., in intellectual property)</strong> - yet R&amp;D and IP teams spend <strong>half their time buried in manual work</strong>, sifting through patents and paperwork instead of pushing the frontier forward. The tools of creating and protecting are stuck in the past. <strong>We’re here to fix that.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ankar is building the R&amp;D tools for the AI era and defining what applied research will look like in the next 20 years</strong>. We’re building infrastructure and product experiences our customers rely on every day. You’ll translate messy, ambiguous problems into clean, dependable software—and you’ll do it at the cutting-edge of AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re at an inflection point:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We’ve raised &gt;$24M to date from Tier-1 VCs</strong> like Atomico, Index Ventures, Norrsken, Daphni, and angels like the Founder of Hugging Face, CEO from Datadog, and Leaders from DeepMind and OpenAI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We’re already working with the world’s most innovative companies</strong> including Fortune 500 company <strong>L’Oréal</strong> and global law firm <strong>Vorys</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Expanding our world-class team</strong> with alumni from <strong>Palantir, Amazon, and BCG</strong> to tackle the <strong>$1T+ innovation market</strong>. We’re just getting started.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll be doing</strong><br />We’re looking for a patent professional with deep large-molecule life sciences expertise who can bridge product development, engineering and IP protection. You’ll work hands-on with pharmaceutical and biotech customers to design AI-powered patent solutions that understand the nuances of biologics—including antibodies, proteins, peptides, nucleic acids, vaccines and cell and gene therapies—and the conventions that govern their patent protection.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build life sciences-specific patent products:</strong> Partner with product and engineering teams to develop AI tools tailored to large-molecule patents—from protein and antibody sequence analysis to biologics claim generation, sequence-listing support and prior-art searching across life sciences databases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Embed with pharmaceutical and biotech customers:</strong> Work directly with in-house patent counsel and prosecution teams to design, prototype and deploy high-value proofs of concept for large-molecule patent workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape product development with biologics expertise:</strong> Translate complex large-molecule patent challenges into product requirements, ensuring our AI understands sequence data, CDR and epitope definitions, functional claim language, sequence variants, experimental data and biologics drafting conventions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive customer success in large-molecule patents:</strong> Lead technical sessions with patent professionals to ensure our products deliver measurable value across biologics patent portfolios.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Identify emerging biologics patent opportunities:</strong> Recognize evolving needs across therapeutic antibodies, recombinant proteins, vaccines, nucleic acid technologies, cell and gene therapies, biologics formulations and regulatory IP strategy.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Large-molecule patent expertise:</strong> At least two years of experience in biologics patent prosecution, pharmaceutical or biotech IP, or other large-molecule-focused patent work, with a strong understanding of the patent lifecycle from invention disclosure through prosecution, grant and enforcement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical life sciences foundation:</strong> Strong knowledge of molecular biology, biochemistry, immunology or a related discipline, including an understanding of protein and nucleic acid sequences, antibody structure and function, biologics development, and how these translate into patentable subject matter.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong biologics drafting skills:</strong> Experience developing claim strategies for antibodies, proteins, nucleic acids or other biologic modalities, with an understanding of written-description, enablement, sequence-listing and functional-claiming requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Builder’s mindset:</strong> You thrive in ambiguity, iterate quickly on prototypes and enjoy creating order from complexity. You can move seamlessly between high-level patent strategy and detailed biologics claim construction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Extreme ownership:</strong> You anticipate problems, take responsibility for outcomes and consistently deliver. This is how you grow—and how we win.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>[Bonus points]:</strong> Experience at a patent law firm representing pharmaceutical or biotech clients; in-house patent counsel experience at a pharmaceutical or biotech company; expertise in emerging modalities such as antibody-drug conjugates, bispecific antibodies, RNA therapeutics or cell and gene therapies; or an advanced life sciences degree combined with patent training.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>This role is not for you if... </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You need a highly structured environment, a predefined playbook, regular working hours, or a schedule that never requires travel. We operate with high autonomy and ownership, expect our team to go above and beyond, be obsessed with our mission and thrive in ambiguity rather than wait for direction.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You prefer long planning cycles and certainty before acting. We move quickly, ship often, and adapt based on customer feedback and new information.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want to manage the work rather than do the work. We're builders first, and everyone is expected to contribute directly to creating exceptional products.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take it personally when ideas are challenged, priorities shift, or work gets redirected. We care more about finding the right answer than defending a particular one.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we put behind our people</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building at the frontier takes exceptional people. We invest accordingly.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Health Insurance : </strong>Full private health &amp; dental coverage for you and your dependents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension: </strong>Flexible pension scheme with up to 5% employer matching on qualifying earnings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Food on us: </strong>Team lunches twice a week, plus dinner when working late in the office.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cycle to work: </strong>Green Commute initiative scheme (up to £3k) to help you get a new bike tax-free.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Way we work: </strong>We combine deep, in-person collaboration (3 days/week in our Shoreditch office) with flexibility and trust. What matters is ownership, impact, and results, not where you work from.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Visa sponsorship:</strong> Yes</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/ankar/patent-engineer-life-sciences-london-142371","tags":["Go-to-Market & Customer Innovation"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793504415},{"slug":"gtm-lead-uk-smb-mm-enterprise-london-179222","company_name":"Dust","title":"GTM Lead, UK - SMB/MM/Enterprise","description":"<h1><strong>About Dust</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work is being rewritten, and the people holding the pen are the ones who actually run it.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With enterprise-grade governance, flexible model choice, and a collaborative interface for humans and agents to work together, Dust empowers AI Operators at the world’s fastest-moving companies to rewire how work gets done.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With 70%+ weekly active users, people stick with Dust as much as they do with Slack and Notion. We don't get piloted and shelved. We land once, and spread. <strong>We're at an exciting stage of our journey, and growing fast.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're serving <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://dust.tt/customers">great customers</a> like Datadog, 1Password, Cursor, Clay, Vanta and Persona, and aim to x5 our growth by the end of 2026.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dust is backed by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://techcrunch.com/2024/06/27/dust-grabs-another-16-million-for-its-enterprise-ai-assistants-connected-to-internal-data/">Sequoia</a> with a determined team of optimists (coming from Stripe, OpenAI, and Stanford) who like to focus on users, ship fast, and don't take themselves too seriously while doing so. The Generalist <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/dust-tt_were-honored-to-be-recognized-on-the-generalists-activity-7359284343929741313-Rq04">named us among the Future 50</a>.</p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re hiring a hands-on sales leader for the UK. You’ll build, lead, and coach the regional Sales team, deliver against ARR and pipeline goals, and build a repeatable local growth engine.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll act as the business lead for your market, with accountability for revenue. As a sales leader, you'll lead and coach the sales team, stay close to customers and deals, and build a repeatable sales approach that fits your market. As an orchestrator, you'll coordinate the local pipeline generation activities that feed your number, including marketing and pre-sales. You'll work closely with leaders across BDR, Growth, Field Marketing, Partnerships, Revenue Operations, Solutions Engineering, Deployment, and Customer Success, and influence how they support your market's priorities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the region’s ARR plan, forecast, and qualified pipeline. Work with the CRO to set priorities, understand capacity needs, and support the team to deliver against the plan.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and lead the regional Sales team. Hire, onboard, coach, and develop sellers, while staying hands-on in priority opportunities from prospecting and discovery through qualification, evaluation, negotiation, and close.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make clear, evidence-based recommendations to Product based on regional customer conversations, deal patterns, and market needs. Build and refine a repeatable regional sales approach using pipeline, win/loss learning, and customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive the plan in partnership with field marketing to set priorities for events, campaigns, customer advocacy and community programs, and direct how field marketing resources are used to support your pipeline and ARR goals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the marketing leadership, who own field marketing standards, methods and team management, to make sure regional programs are well executed, measured and consistent with Dust's broader marketing approach</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with BDR and Growth leaders to build a qualified pipeline through a deliberate mix of outbound and other locally effective channels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set direction for how Partnerships can support regional priorities. Work with the Partnerships lead to identify opportunities for sourcing, co-selling, or delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate with Solutions Engineering, Deployment, Professional Services, and Customer Success to support credible evaluations, successful implementations, customer outcomes, and expansion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent regional customer needs internally and share market learning with the CRO and functional leaders, contributing to consistent GTM practices across Dust.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Market-specific focus</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>United Kingdom</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build on early customer and partner traction. Use customer referrals, targeted events, and focused market experiments to build qualified pipeline and strengthen local customer proof.</p><h3></h3><h2><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven sales professional who has grown from individual contributor into people leadership, with 5+ years leading B2B software sales and coaching regional sales teams and a hands-on understanding of how to help reps succeed in-market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've owned a market or segment revenue number end to end, not just a team's quota. You've built pipeline through functions you didn't manage, such as marketing, partners and pre-sales, and you've made real calls about where capacity and budget go, including between direct sales and partners</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to lead by example in priority opportunities, from discovery through close.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building pipeline and customer relationships in a market where the brand or sales motion is still developing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A disciplined approach to forecasting and performance feedback, paired with high EQ and a genuinely supportive leadership style.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An appetite for building, testing, and refining a market over multiple quarters while balancing near-term results with durable growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What success looks like</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The region delivers against its ARR and pipeline goals while developing a repeatable sales approach suited to local customers. The team builds customer trust and referenceable outcomes, cross-functional support is focused on regional priorities, and market learning informs Dust’s broader GTM approach.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Location</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're prioritizing building our team with an in-person culture at our offices in Paris, London, San Francisco, and New York because we value the magic that happens when talented people work closely together.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have an office-first culture. Some of the best things about building at Dust are the energy, the fast decisions, and the unexpected conversations that unlock a hard problem, which happen because we are in the same room. Being together is not a formality, it is how we do our best work, and it is something we actively protect.<br /><br />That said, we hire people with strong judgement and we extend that trust to how they manage their time. When working from home makes more sense for what you need to get done that day, we trust you to make that call.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Why Dust</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The models are powerful enough. What's missing is the product layer where AI meets how companies actually work. That's what we're building: the infrastructure that lets any team turn scattered knowledge and tools into coordinated execution with agents they build, own, and run themselves.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use Dust ourselves every day. We get to shape how humans and agents collaborate while solving our own problems with the product we ship. That loop is rare, and it's why we move fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited about defining a new category and want to join a determined team of optimists who focus on users, ship fast, and don't take themselves too seriously, we'd love to talk.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Even if you don't check every box in our requirements, we encourage you to apply. We value diverse perspectives and backgrounds, and we're more interested in your potential and passion than a perfect match to our checklist. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learn how we think and work.</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://blog.dust.tt/a-first-version-of-our-product-constitution/">Our product constitution,</a> <em>a story about our mission</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="break-all font-semibold transition-all duration-200 ease-in-out hover:underline text-highlight hover:text-highlight-400 active:text-highlight-dark" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xIvlRWEXqqw">Your Next Co-Worker Isn’t Human</a>, <strong>Stanislas Polu</strong>, VivaTech 2026. A conversation about AI agents taking on larger parts of work and how teams collaborate with them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="break-all font-semibold transition-all duration-200 ease-in-out hover:underline text-highlight hover:text-highlight-400 active:text-highlight-dark" href="https://www.nasdaq.com/videos/dust">Dust: Gabriel Hubert on Enterprise AI</a>, <strong>Gabriel Hubert</strong>, Nasdaq, published May 7, 2026. On Dust’s approach to enterprise AI and building the company in Europe.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/dust/gtm-lead-uk-smb-mm-enterprise-london-179222","tags":["Sale