&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is what you move:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Manager Media Solutions | Campaign (m/f/d)&lt;/strong&gt;, you are responsible for the operational planning, coordination, and activation of digital campaigns for our&amp;nbsp;key global client Roche.&amp;nbsp;Your primary focus is on programmatic activations across CTV, Video, and DOOH. Based in the Media Solutions Unit Switzerland, you will work closely with Client Leads, Programmatic Specialists, local and international WPP teams, as well as publishers and technology partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Campaign Activation:&lt;/strong&gt; Independently coordinate and activate programmatic campaigns with a clear focus on CTV, Video, and DOOH.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;International Campaign Roll-outs:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the execution of multinational campaigns across various markets, working closely with local WPP teams to identify the best publishers, ad inventories, and activation opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Setup, Monitoring &amp;amp; Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Campaign setup in relevant DSPs and activation platforms is in your hands, along with continuous delivery monitoring and data-driven performance optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner &amp;amp; Client Team Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a central interface with publishers, media vendors, and technology partners while advising client teams on feasibility checks and activation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting &amp;amp; Insights:&lt;/strong&gt; Derive actionable insights from campaign reports and share best practices across involved teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Processes &amp;amp; Innovation:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively document and enhance activation processes, drive competency growth in Programmatic, CTV, and DOOH, and contribute to evaluating new technologies as well as international projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The following qualities distinguish you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programmatic &amp;amp; Media Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid professional experience in digital media, programmatic advertising, campaign management, or ad operations – ideally within an agency, media owner, or adtech environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform &amp;amp; AdTech Know-how:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with at least one leading DSP (e.g., DV360, The Trade Desk, Adform) along with a strong understanding of digital advertising ecosystems and adtech infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CTV &amp;amp; DOOH Specialization:&lt;/strong&gt; Prior exposure to Connected TV (CTV), Digital Video, and/or Digital Out-of-Home (DOOH), combined with an enthusiasm for cross-channel digital campaign formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organization &amp;amp; Project Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong organizational skills, a structured and solution-oriented work approach, and ease in managing complex campaign workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management &amp;amp; Team Spirit:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent communication skills, analytical thinking, and a collaborative mindset for cross-market teamwork in an international environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Business-fluent English (written and spoken) for daily international collaboration; good German skills are a welcome plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Furthermore you are:&lt;strong&gt; #problem-solver #team-player #hands-on-mentality&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this job sounds exciting to you, we strongly encourage you to apply, even if you don&#39;t have every qualification listed above.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at WPP Media:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our passion for shaping the next era of media includes investing in our employees to help them do their best work, and we’re just as committed to employee growth as we are to responsible media investment. WPP Media employees can tap into the global WPP Media &amp;amp; WPP networks to pursue their passions, grow their networks, and learn at the cutting edge of marketing and advertising. We have a variety of employee resource groups and host frequent in-office events showcasing team wins, sharing thought leadership, and celebrating holidays and milestone events.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP Media is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to particular characteristics. We are committed to fostering a culture of respect in which everyone feels they belong and has the same opportunities to progress in their careers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please read our privacy policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for Germany, Austria and Switzerland for further information on how we process the data you provide. #LI-Promoted 14018&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-CA&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot;&gt;Please read our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy-policy#:~:text=WPP%20Media%20Privacy%20Notice%20for%20Recruitment&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-CA&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot;&gt;for more information on how we process the information you provide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:276}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/wppmedia/manager-media-solutions-campaign-zurich-379570","tags":["Media Management & Delivery"],"job_types":[],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1793483719},{"slug":"intern-electrical-rd-engineer-satigny-194732","company_name":"Secheron S Dot A","title":"Intern Electrical R&D Engineer","description":"<p>With over 140 years of Swiss engineering heritage, Sécheron Hasler Group is a global leader in high-power electrical and electronic equipment. Our solutions power railways, renewable energy, DC and AC networks, and industrial systems worldwide trusted for their precision, reliability, and innovation.</p><p>Safety meets innovation in our Electrical Safety Solutions unit. From high-speed circuit breakers to voltage limiters, we engineer the components that protect critical infrastructure. Be part of a team where your work safeguards lives and powers progress.</p><p>We are looking for a talented Electrical Engineer student or recent graduate for an internship of at least 6 months in our AC Circuit Breaker team located in Satigny (Geneva). You will get a hands on opportunity to join an innovative developing project, for AC medium voltage devices.</p><p></p><h3>Main tasks:</h3><ul><li>Provide technical design inputs for HV insulators&nbsp;/ Circuit breakers</li><li>Develop FEM models, perform simulations, and document the results&nbsp;</li><li>Review drawings and provide feedback, verify bills of materials</li><li>Conduct patent searches and summarize relevant findings&nbsp;</li><li>Assist during tests, write reports</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><h3>Mandatory:</h3><ul><li>Last year as a master student or recently graduated</li><li>English fluency</li><li>Finite element analysis coursework</li></ul><p></p><h3>Nice to have:</h3><ul><li>French fluency</li><li>Any hands-on experience/ relevant projects in high voltage components (bushing, switchgear, insulators, cables)</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p>We foster&nbsp;flat hierarchies&nbsp;and&nbsp;direct communication, enabling quick decisions and strong collaboration across all levels. You’ll be trusted with real responsibility and encouraged to take initiative, with plenty of opportunities to grow both personally and professionally.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/secheron-s-dot-a/intern-electrical-rd-engineer-satigny-194732","tags":["Engineering","Electrical/Electronic Manufacturing","Sécheron | Electrical Safety Solutions"],"job_types":["internship"],"location":"Satigny, Switzerland","created_at":1793481616},{"slug":"remote-influencer-marketing-manager-switzerland-398870","company_name":"Hilobyaktiia","title":"Influencer Marketing Manager (m/f/d)","description":"<p><u><strong>About Hilo by Aktiia</strong></u></p><p>High blood pressure is the world's most common disease, causing 18M deaths each year.&nbsp;At Hilo by&nbsp;Aktiia,&nbsp;we're&nbsp;building a world where no lives are lost to its effects — with technology that helps people take control of their health.&nbsp;</p><p>We're&nbsp;a venture-backed scale-up with $96M raised from investors in Europe and the US. Rooted in 18 years of research at the Swiss Center for Electronics and Microtechnology (CSEM), our device is the world's only medically accurate, cuffless, continuous blood pressure monitor for daily use — clinically validated and CE Marked as a Class IIa medical device, now available in 12 countries. In July, we launched in the US.&nbsp;</p><p>We're&nbsp;a&nbsp;remote-first&nbsp;company headquartered in Neuchâtel, Switzerland, united by our passion for impact and innovation. Applicants must already hold a valid visa or work permit for their country of residence, as Hilo is not able to provide visa sponsorship.</p><p><u><strong><br>Role Overview</strong></u></p><p>As Influencer Marketing Manager, you will develop and run Hilo’s influencer marketing program across our key markets. You will find creators whose voices and audiences fit our brand, negotiate effective partnerships, and shape content that makes Hilo relevant and credible. The role combines brand and performance: you will use data to estimate the potential of each partnership before we invest, measure its results, and apply what you learn to future campaigns.</p><p>Work location: Our company operates on a remote-first model. This role can be performed remotely from anywhere in Europe. Fluent English and German are a must. Occasional travel to our office in Neuchâtel, Switzerland, or to team events may be required.</p><h3><u>Core Responsibilities</u></h3><ul><li>Identify, assess, and recruit creators across relevant platforms and markets.</li><li>Develop campaign concepts that balance Hilo’s brand goals with measurable commercial outcomes.</li><li>Forecast likely reach, engagement, traffic, and acquisition outcomes to guide creator selection and budgets.</li><li>Negotiate fees, deliverables, timelines, and content usage rights, including rights to use creator content in paid campaigns.</li><li>Manage partnerships end to end, from briefing and content review through publication and reporting.</li><li>Build and nurture long-term relationships with creators and brand ambassadors to drive sustained awareness, trust, and advocacy.</li><li>Collaborate with paid media teams to amplify high-performing creator content across paid social and other relevant channels.</li><li>Set clear goals, track brand and performance metrics, and compare results with initial estimates.</li><li>Use campaign data and audience insights to improve creator selection, content formats, and investment decisions.</li><li>Work across marketing and product to align campaigns with Hilo’s priorities and approved health claims.</li><li>Build repeatable processes that support growth across the US, UK, Germany, and other markets.</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><u><strong>Background &amp; Experience</strong></u></p><ul><li>At least 2 years of hands-on influencer or creator marketing experience, including managing partnerships from start to finish.</li><li>A data-driven mindset: you can estimate campaign outcomes, assess performance, and turn findings into better decisions.</li><li>Strong creative judgment and an understanding of how creator content builds both brand trust and customer demand.</li><li>Strong negotiation skills and confidence working with creators and their representatives.</li><li>Excellent communication, organization, and attention to detail.</li><li>Fluency in English; German is a plus.</li><li>Experience in health tech, wellness, medical devices, or another category where trust and accurate claims matter is welcome.</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p><u><strong>What Makes You A Great Fit</strong></u></p><h3>At Hilo by Aktiia, our values guide everything we do:&nbsp;</h3><p><strong>Move the Needle</strong> — You focus on what truly drives impact for our customers and company. You use data and clarity to guide your decisions and prioritize what matters most. You push boundaries with bold, thoughtful innovation and hold yourself accountable for results.</p><p><strong>Move Fast, Learn, Refine</strong> — You work with urgency and purpose, balancing speed with high quality. You treat mistakes as learning opportunities, experiment thoughtfully and iterate quickly. You take ownership, act hands-on and always look for smarter, faster ways to get things done, including leveraging AI and new tools.</p><p><strong>Team First</strong> — You put the team above individual interests, building trust through openness and respect. You encourage healthy debate, challenge directly while caring personally and stand behind team decisions. You act as an owner, stepping in when needed and doing what’s necessary for the team’s success.</p><p><u><strong>Why Join Us?</strong></u></p><ul><li>Hilo by Aktiia is becoming one of the most important med-tech companies and you can be part of this exciting story.</li><li>Work on a mission that matters: transforming cardiovascular health at global scale.</li><li>Be part of a high-impact, fast-growing, and venture-backed scale-up company.</li><li>Collaborate with a diverse, passionate and talented team.</li><li>Competitive compensation, equity program and other benefits (depending on location).</li></ul><h3><strong>Ready to Move the Needle?</strong></h3><p>If you are passionate about making a meaningful impact in people's lives and excel in an environment where individuals take ownership and are committed to delivering results, we are happy to receive your application.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/hilobyaktiia/remote-influencer-marketing-manager-switzerland-398870","tags":["Marketing","Medical Devices","Marketing/Brand","Remote"],"job_types":["Full time","mid-senior"],"location":"Switzerland","created_at":1793449209},{"slug":"electronics-engineer-freienbach-418073","company_name":"3Brain AG","title":"Electronics Engineer","description":"<p>3Brain is a Swiss deep tech company working on cell-electronic interfaces that link biological networks to computers via custom-made semiconductor microchips. Our mission is to empower life scientists to probe intelligent networks, accelerate biomedical discoveries for the benefit of patients, and create a future more exciting than the present. Our interdisciplinary team of scientists and engineers are constantly pushing the boundaries of engineering for life’s complexities. We are ambitious, fast-growing and love to explore. The company’s cutting-edge products are used in laboratories and pharma companies worldwide. 3Brain is headquartered in Switzerland nearby Zurich, has a Data Science and Discovery Unit in Genova, Italy, and an operational unit in the US.</p><h2>Tasks</h2><p>For the next expansion step, 3Brain is looking for a full-time Hardware electronics engineer to reinforce our R&D team. You will help develop embedded systems for high-speed data acquisition devices, including tasks such as system engineering, schematics design and layout, testing and verification. You will also contribute to the current device’s life-cycle management, including activities such as automation, production testing and optimization.</p><p>In particular, your tasks involve:</p><ul><li><p>Designing high-speed embedded systems and architectures for products based on high-resolution microelectrode arrays</p></li><li><p>Designing low-level current/voltage instrumentation tools to operate Micro-electrode Arrays (MEA)</p></li><li><p>Design and implement hardware systems and sub-systems (PCBs), including high-speed ADCs, microcontrollers and FPGA-SoMs, power supplies, etc.</p></li><li><p>Bringing-up, testing, measuring, characterization and validation of electronic systems</p></li><li><p>Design and development of production test tools</p></li><li><p>Make, assemble, debug and test demonstrators and prototype devices</p></li><li><p>Documentation (engineering, production, QA, etc.)</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><p><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></p><ul><li><p>Independence and ability to communicate and work effectively with other team members in a multicultural and international environment</p></li><li><p>BSc/MSc in Electrical Engineering</p></li><li><p>Minimum of 5 years of professional experience in HW Design</p></li><li><p>Design of analog electronics and high-speed digital systems (Simulation, Schematics, HDI Layout)</p></li><li><p>Detailed understanding of PCB-manufacturing</p></li><li><p>Good understanding of EMC compliance and mechanical integration</p></li><li><p>Practical and industrial hands-on experience (e.g. prototype soldering, setting up test-benches, transfer and scale-up to mass production, etc.)</p></li><li><p>Prototyping and testing (i.e. for bring-up, debugging and production)</p></li><li><p>Background in basic signal processing (i.e. sampling, filtering, aliasing, etc.)</p></li><li><p>Fluency in English</p></li></ul><p><strong>Additional Qualifications</strong></p><ul><li><p>Knowledge of Python</p></li><li><p>Microprocessor programming</p></li></ul><h2>Benefits</h2><ul><li><p>A dynamic and stimulating work environment driven by a desire to build transformational technologies to help others.</p></li><li><p>A young, fast-growing company with plenty of opportunities for personal growth and development.</p></li><li><p>Great challenges and adventures in both technical and economical fields.</p></li><li><p>Working place: <strong>Pfäffikon SZ, Switzerland</strong>. It is a lakeside village just outside of Zurich, the country’s main cultural, financial and business center.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/3brain-ag/electronics-engineer-freienbach-418073","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Indefinite contract (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Freienbach","created_at":1793437240},{"slug":"projektleiter-ib-risiken-tradingdesk-zurich-213458","company_name":"coni+partner AG","title":"Projektleiter IB / Risiken Tradingdesk","description":"<p>coni + partner ist ein seit 1993 bestehendes Beratungshaus mit Sitz in Zürich und Niederlassungen in Düsseldorf und Shanghai. Unsere Stärke ist die passgenaue Besetzung von Positionen entsprechend der Unternehmenskultur, unter genauer Betrachtung fachlicher Kompetenzen, Referenzen und «soft skills» der Kandidaten.</p><p>Unser Kunde ist das IB eines internationalen Bankkonzerns in Zürich. Wir suchen einen Spezialisten (m, f, d) als</p><p><strong>Projektleiter IB / Risiken Tradingdesk</strong></p><p>Ihre Aufgaben:</p><p>Projektleitung/Teilprojektleitung bei Run- & Change-the-Bank-Projekten mit regulatorischem Fokus für das Tradingdesk /  Durchführung von Compliance Reviews / Verantwortlich für Weisungen / Support bei der Umsetzung von Projektentscheiden / Maintenance von Manualen /  Ansprechpartner für Compliance-Anfragen und Kommunikation mit Gegenparteien, Banken, Brokern, Regulatoren etc. / Organisation und Leitung von Schulungen sowie Teilnahme an Workshops als Referent. / Deutsch und Englisch. </p><p>Ihr Profil:</p><p>Master oder Bachelor in Banking und Finance oder Wirtschaftswissenschaften / Weiterbildung in Compliance, Risk Management oder Projektleitung / Erfahrung mit Compliance des Tradingdesks einer Bank / Interesse an bankinternen Prozessen und an regulatorischen Fragestellungen / Lösungs- und kundenorientierte sowie sorgfältige und analytische Arbeitsweise / Eigeninitiative, Flexibilität, diplomatisches Verhandlungsgeschick und hohes Verantwortungsbewusstsein / Kommunikative, selbständige, teamfähige, belastbare und durchsetzungsfähige Persönlichkeit / Sprachen Deutsch und Englisch.</p><p>Ihr Kontakt:</p><p>Herr Ivano Coni ist gerne für Sie da. Ihre Bewerbung wird streng vertraulich behandelt.</p><p></p><p><strong>coni + partner ag</strong></p><p>Ivano Coni</p><p>Managing Director</p><p>Klosbachstrasse 107</p><p>CH-8032 -----<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/conipartner-ag/projektleiter-ib-risiken-tradingdesk-zurich-213458","tags":["Project Management"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag","berufserfahren"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1793430039},{"slug":"relationship-manager-for-external-asset-managers-m-f-d-zurich-57491","company_name":"coni+partner AG","title":"Relationship Manager for External Asset Managers","description":"<p>coni + partner, established 1993, is a consultancy company with headquarters in Zurich and subsidiaries in Düsseldorf and Shanghai. We are specialised in custom-fit staffing in tune with the corporate culture by ensuring a perfect match of professional skills, references and personal as well as social skills of successful candidates.</p><p>Our client is the private banking an international bank in Zurich. We are searching for a relationship manager for EAM (m, f, d) as</p><p><strong>Relationship Manager for External Asset Managers </strong></p><p>Your Tasks: </p><p>As an Account Manager, you will be responsible for supporting external asset managers (EAM) / Independently managing, expanding, and maintaining an EAM client portfolio / Supporting EAM clients in developing solutions and processes—both in collaboration with the Advisory and Research teams to create customized investment solutions, and with Risk Management and IT / Reviewing and monitoring client orders / Monitoring credit lines and investment maturities / Overseeing administrative matters / Maintaining professional communication, providing prompt service, and marketing the services offered / Ensuring a high standard of service as the foundation for sustainable client relationships / Managing retrocessions and associated commissions / Periodically reviewing the EAM client portfolio, including the evaluation of EAM clients / Continuous acquisition and onboarding of new EAM clients / Regular review and optimization of the service portfolio and collaboration on the further development of marketing events / Ensuring compliance with EAM clients based on legal requirements such as KYC/AML, FATCA/CRS, MiFID, etc. / Advising EAM clients based on the bank’s compliance standards and in accordance with best practices / Planning and conducting training sessions as needed.</p><p>Your Profile:</p><p>HF, Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Banking & Finance / AZEK, CFA, or CWMA certification preferred / Solid experience in serving EAM clients / Proven track record of building new client relationships / Sales-oriented mindset and entrepreneurial thinking / Ability to identify and interpret client needs / In-depth knowledge of investment products across all asset classes and the composition of investment portfolios / Strong service orientation with a focus on fast turnaround times and high quality / In-depth knowledge of compliance, including cross-border matters / Integrity, initiative, a high level of commitment, and a strong sense of responsibility / Strong interpersonal skills and an aptitude for multitasking / Interest in giving presentations / Proficiency with IT and Microsoft Office / German and English.</p><p>Your Contact:</p><p> Mr. Ivano Coni would like to support you. Your application will be kept strictly confidential.</p><p></p><p><strong>coni + partner ag</strong></p><p>Ivano Coni</p><p>Managing Director</p><p>Klosbachstrasse 107</p><p>CH-8032 Zürich</p><p> contact -----<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/conipartner-ag/relationship-manager-for-external-asset-managers-m-f-d-zurich-57491","tags":["Asset","Fonds Management"],"job_types":["Indefinite contract (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1793520140},{"slug":"head-fund-operations-control-middle-office-zurich-391727","company_name":"coni+partner AG","title":"Head Fund Operations Control / Middle Office","description":"<p>coni + partner, established 1993, is a consultancy company with headquarters in Zurich and subsidiaries in Düsseldorf and Shanghai. We are specialised in custom-fit staffing in tune with the corporate culture by ensuring a perfect match of professional skills, references and personal as well as social skills of successful candidates.</p><p>Our client is the asset management an international bank in Zurich. We are searching for a team leader (m, f, d) as</p><p><strong>Head Fund Operations Control / Middle Office</strong></p><p>Your Tasks: </p><p>Within the asset management middle office, responsible for the investment fund sector (CISA, ETF, UCITS), overseeing the reliability of data flows within the department and to custodian banks or companies providing outsourced fund services to banks or fund managers / Responsible for concepts, specifications, analyses, best practice as well as leading and developing a team / Responsible for supervising data quality, NAV calculations, fund key figures, cost transparency, PRIIP Key Information Documents, factsheet production and the preparation of fund reports / Responsible for valuation decisions and involvement in committees and bodies / Collaborating with various specialist teams and monitoring regulatory requirements / Planning and implementing optimisation projects with internal and external stakeholders, as well as further developing and automating processes and services within Fund Operations / Ad hoc projects.</p><p>Your Profil