rd and risk assessments, define certification strategies across international markets (EU, North America, marine), and interface directly with notified bodies and classification societies to ensure our fuel cell systems are safe, fully compliant, and market-ready.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role <strong>requires a full-time, on-site presence at our office in Nyon, Switzerland</strong>. We are <strong>unable to offer remote or hybrid arrangements</strong>, so candidates should be based locally or <strong>prepared to relocate</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Key responsibilities</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Certification strategy and project management</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify applicable directives, regulations, harmonised standards and class rules early in the development cycle and translate them into design requirements (EU, North America, marine)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Select and manage notified bodies, NRTLs, classification societies and test laboratories, own budgets, schedules and contracts for certification work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and witness type tests, factory acceptance tests (FAT) and site acceptance tests (SAT)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Safety engineering and risk analysis</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead risk assessments to ISO 12100 and hazard studies (HAZID, HAZOP to IEC 61882)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead design and process FMEA (IEC 60812) for stacks, balance of plant, containers and fuel processing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run explosion-protection assessments: hazardous area classification (IEC 60079-10-1), ventilation and gas detection concepts, and equipment selection</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Specify and verify safety functions to ISO 13849 (PL) and IEC 61508, including safety requirement specifications and validation reports</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compliance and technical documentation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compile and maintain technical construction files, CE Declarations of Conformity, type-approval dossiers and certification reports</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and review user, installation, operation and maintenance manuals, safety instructions and labelling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain the standards register and assess the impact of new or revised standards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage certification change control: assess design changes for impact on existing certificates</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaboration and continuous improvement</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the internal authority on certification scope: ensure in-service conformity of series production with certified designs, and support procurement and supply chain on material and packaging compliance (e.g. RoHS, packaging regulations).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support design reviews and supplier qualification, including component certificates (ATEX, PED, electrical)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Standards and regulatory scope</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role covers, but is not limited to, the frameworks below. Working knowledge of most is expected; deep expertise in several is required</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">IEC 62282 series, CSA/ANSI FC 1:2021, ISO 16110-1 and Machinery Regulation (EU) 2023/1230</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Required qualifications</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Master’s or bachelor’s degree in mechanical, electrical, chemical, process or safety engineering, or equivalent</p></li><li><p style="min-heigh