.</p></li><li><p>Du setzt Agentic-Testing-Ansätze in Kundenprojekten um.</p></li><li><p>Du berätst Kunden bei Toolauswahl, Architektur und Automatisierungsstrategie.</p></li></ul><h2>Das bringst du mit</h2><ul><li><p>Du verfügst über mehrere aktuelle UiPath-Zertifizierungen, darunter mindestens eine auf Professional-Level, z. B. Automation Developer Professional oder Test Automation Engineer Professional.</p></li><li><p>Du hast mindestens 3 Jahre Praxiserfahrung mit UiPath, vor allem in der Testautomatisierung, und hast Lösungen eigenständig umgesetzt.</p></li><li><p>Du hast Erfahrung in der Beratung von Kunden und Stakeholdern, kommunizierst fliessend auf Englisch und bist motiviert, deine Deutschkenntnisse weiter auszubauen.</p></li><li><p>Du bist bereit, in der gesamten Deutschschweiz bei Kunden vor Ort zu arbeiten.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Das bringst du idealerweise zusätzlich mit</strong></p><ul><li><p>UiPath Agentic Automation Associate oder weitere Zertifizierungen aus dem UiPath-Portfolio</p></li><li><p>ISTQB Foundation Level oder weiterführende ISTQB-Zertifizierungen</p></li><li><p>Erfahrung mit CI/CD-Umgebungen wie Azure DevOps, GitLab oder Jenkins</p></li><li><p>Grundkenntnisse in C# oder VB.NET</p></li><li><p>Erfahrung mit weiteren Testtools wie Tricentis Tosca oder Playwright</p></li></ul><h2>Deine ersten Monate bei Infometis</h2><p>Du startest nach Vereinbarung in eine unbefristete Anstellung mit drei Monaten Probezeit. Je nach Projekt arbeitest du schon früh direkt beim Kunden. Dabei hast du ein Team im Rücken, das dich stärkt. Bei Fragen helfen sich die Infometen und Infometinnen untereinander schnell und unkompliziert, auch über Projekte hinweg.</p><h2>Wie sieht der Bewerbungsprozess aus?</h2><p>Bis Ende November sammeln wir alle Bewerbungen und sehen sie uns sorgfältig an. Im Dezember starten wir mit den Interviews. Passt dein Profil, melden wir uns bei dir für einen Termin. Schick uns deine Bewerbung deshalb am besten bis <strong>Ende November</strong>.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><ul><li><p>Sozialleistungen: Du profitierst von überdurchschnittlichen Sozialleistungen.</p></li><li><p>Work-Life-Balance: Geniesse eine 40-Stunden-Woche, die dir genug Raum für Leben neben der Arbeit lässt.</p></li><li><p>Weiterbildungsbudget: Dank einem grosszügigen jährlichen Weiterbildungsbudget bringst du deine Skills auf das nächste Level und kannst dich persönlich weiterentwickeln.</p></li><li><p>Gadgets: Bleibe technisch up-to-date mit einem jährlichen Budget für Gadgets.</p></li><li><p>Team-Events: Von abwechslungsreichen Teamaktivitäten über das Weihnachtsessen bis hin zu unseren regelmässigen Co-Working Days oder Qarterlies: Gemeinsam stärken wir den Zusammenhalt und leben den einzigartigen Infometis-Vibe.</p></li><li><p>Infowell: Profitiere von unserem internen Programm für Betriebliches Gesundheitsmanagement inklusive Plattform für mentale Gesundheit.</p></li><li><p>Zufriedenheit grossgeschrieben: Als «Kununu Top Company 2027» geben wir weiter alles für ein Arbeitsumfeld, in dem du dich wohl fühlst.</p></li></ul><p></p><p></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/infometis-ag/test-automation-engineer-uipath-zurich-440417","tags":["Quality Assurance","Inspection"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag","berufserfahren"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1793360852},{"slug":"software-engineer-net-woerden-145760","company_name":"CCS Connects","title":"Software Engineer (.NET)","description":"<p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Your Mission</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal"><br>As a Software Engineer at CCS, you'll play a key role in our modernization journey—bridging legacy systems with future-ready solutions. You’ll help deliver innovative, high-quality software that transforms how our clients operate. Modernization is not just about adopting new technologies—it’s about continuously improving how we build, learn, and grow. You love experimenting, learning by doing, and inspiring others to raise the bar.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">You’ll join a team focused on modernizing our insurance back-office systems—critical components in our clients' ecosystems.<br>Your main focus will be on <strong>SureCore</strong>, our next-gen solution that works in tandem with <strong>Level</strong>, our trusted legacy platform. This hybrid approach lets us evolve system functionality domain by domain. You enjoy working at the intersection of old and new tech, and you thrive on technical challenges that require creativity and collaboration.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Your Skills &amp; Experience</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Must-have:</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>Strong experience with .NET</p></li><li><p>Hands-on knowledge of Domain-Driven Design (DDD)</p></li><li><p>Comfortable with Docker and container orchestration</p></li><li><p>Proficient in GitHub for version control and collaboration</p></li><li><p>Familiar with both relational and NoSQL databases</p></li><li><p>Understanding of CI/CD pipelines, automation, and cloud-native patterns</p></li><li><p>Excellent team player with clear communication skills and a love for continuous learning</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Nice-to-have:</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>Background in non-life or income insurance</p></li><li><p>Experience with Infrastructure as Code (IaC), preferably Pulumi</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with Azure and/or .NET Aspire</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><ul><li><p>Competitive gross salary: €4,500 – €5,750 per month, depending on experience</p></li><li><p>8.33% holiday allowance and 25 vacation days (option to buy up to 20 extra)</p></li><li><p>Workweek of 32–40 hours, tailored to your needs</p></li><li><p>Laptop and phone provided</p></li><li><p>Remote work expense allowance and budget for an ergonomic home office setup</p></li><li><p>1-year contract with the intention of permanent employment</p></li><li><p>Pension plan with low personal contribution and discounts on group insurance</p></li><li><p>Access to a company fitness program and bike plan</p></li><li><p>Option to work abroad (up to 30 consecutive days per year)</p></li><li><p>Fun team activities organized by our dedicated FUN team</p></li><li><p>A future you build with us: you bring the ambition, we offer the opportunities</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Why Join CCS?</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Because at CCS, work means more than a job. It’s a space to be yourself, make real impact, and keep growing. We're passionate about technology, people, and sustainability—and we believe that work should be filled with purpose, progress, and joy. You’re the missing link in our team. Let’s build the future together. 🚀</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Let’s Connect!</strong></p><p>Are you excited about this position? Apply now with your CV or LinkedIn profile. For questions about the procedure, you can email <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- or call 0348-486848. Acquisition is not appreciated.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/ccs-connects/software-engineer-net-woerden-145760","tags":["Development"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Woerden, Utrecht, Nederland","created_at":1793537492},{"slug":"software-engineer-ii-embedded-platform-den-bosch-78831","company_name":"Hudl","title":"Software Engineer II - Embedded Platform","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Hudl, we build great teams. We hire the best of the best to ensure you’re working with people you can constantly learn from. You’re trusted to get your work done your way while testing the limits of what’s possible and what’s next. We work hard to provide a culture where everyone feels supported, and our employees feel it—their votes helped us become one of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/blog/hudl-2026-top-100-inspiring-workplaces?utm_medium=internal&amp;amp;utm_source=job-ad&amp;amp;utm_campaign=26_NA_talent_job-ad&amp;amp;utm_content=1org_learn-more_blog-link_learn-more_2blog_organic_3ctw&quot;&gt;Top 100 Inspiring Workplaces&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We think of ourselves as the team behind the team, supporting the lifelong impact sports can have: the lessons in teamwork and dedication; the influence of inspiring coaches; and the opportunities to reach new heights. That’s why we help teams from all over the world see their game differently. Our products make it easier for coaches and athletes at any level to capture video, analyze data, share highlights and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ready to join us?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;padding: 56.25% 0 0 0; position: relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://player.vimeo.com/video/1095624224?h=9e8cdc9dbe&amp;amp;badge=0&amp;amp;autopause=0&amp;amp;player_id=0&amp;amp;app_id=58479&quot; width=&quot;&quot; height=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Your Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an Engineer II to join our Platform squad working on one of Hudl’s most innovative products: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/en_gb/products/focus&quot;&gt;next-generation, fully automated sports cameras&lt;/a&gt;. These autonomous cameras use edge AI to automatically track the action and upload to the cloud, giving our customers seamless access to vital, real-time video and insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Platform squad builds the foundation our hardware teams rely on - the build systems, tooling, update pipeline and security processes that take our cameras from development through manufacturing and into the field. As we bring up our next-generation hardware platform, you’ll help shape how it’s built, tested, shipped and kept secure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineer II, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support our hardware squads.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll help hardware squads integrate their work into our CI/CD pipelines, so every change is built, tested and delivered reliably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build development tools.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll create and improve the tools our engineers use every day to build, flash, debug and test devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep our infrastructure running.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll maintain our CI/CD infrastructure, including the regression testing that runs in manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ship updates to the field.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll roll out software updates to our customers’ cameras safely and predictably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable manufacturing.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll provide the tooling our contract manufacturers use to flash, provision and test devices on the production line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the problem.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll work in an autonomous squad that has the freedom and expertise to deliver the best solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Location&lt;/h2&gt;
