esults.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1>Your responsibilites</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Win new strategic customers and grow existing partnerships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build relationships with senior stakeholders and guide them through their SAF journey.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead commercial opportunities from first conversation through to signed agreement, nurturing the relationship at every stage and ensuring a high-quality customer experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop account and engagement plans for high-priority customers and partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create new opportunities through networking, outreach, events, and referrals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share customer and market insights to help continuously improve our commercial approach and propositions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Management of industry initiatives and client-facing campaigns.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with colleagues across SkyNRG to ensure customers receive a seamless experience.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Your profile</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for someone who is commercially sharp, curious by nature, and motivated by helping organisations make meaningful progress towards their sustainability goals.<br /></p><h3>Must-Haves</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8+ years of experience in a consultative B2B business development, sales, or commercial role, preferably within SAF, energy, carbon, or similarly complex or emerging markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven track record of developing new business and converting strategic opportunities into commercial partnerships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and maintaining relationships with senior stakeholders and decision-makers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading complex commercial discussions and contract negotiations involving multiple stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong commercial judgment and the ability to balance customer needs with business objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical skills and attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with CRM systems and data-driven business development processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability and motivation to quickly build expertise in SAF, SAF certificates, and the evolving regulatory landscape.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A continuous improvement mindset, and willingness to act as an ambassador for SkyNRG and its values: Driven, Genuine, Change-maker</p></li></ul><h3>Nice-to-Haves</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in SAF, aviation,  carbon markets or related sectors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in a scale-up or fast-growing business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with HubSpot.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A relevant professional network that can help open doors and create opportunities.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>About SkyNRG</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since 2009, SkyNRG has been a change maker in the aviation industry. We are dedicated to supplying and producing high-integrity Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF), making sustainable aviation a reality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaboration is fundamental to achieving our ambition. We nurture genuine relationships with global partners in our drive to make SAF <em>the</em> alternative to fossil jet fuel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our in-house team of SAF experts have helped over 60 airlines and corporates reduce their climate impact using the Book &amp; Claim mechanism; the most transparent and traceable way to support aviation sustainability with real emission reductions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sustainability is woven into the fabric of our company. We maintain an independent Sustainability Board, which advises the company on feedstocks and provides strategic guidance on wide-ranging sustainability issues. SkyNRG operations are certified against the RSB EU RED, CORSIA, and Book &amp; Claim standards.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">At SkyNRG, you’ll find:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An innovation-driven culture – where big ideas turn into real impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth opportunities – in a fast-scaling, industry-changing company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative team – where your ideas and expertise are valued</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A mission that matters – leading the change in the energy transition by producing and supplying high-integrity SAF</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>What we offer</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a brand-new office in the heart of Amsterdam, designed for collaboration and creativity. Most importantly, you’ll have the opportunity to contribute to a truly game-changing green initiative, making a real impact on the aviation industry and the planet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Besides that, we offer:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30 paid holidays + 2 for choosing sustainable travel options for your holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to a sustainable organization (B Corp)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Attractive bonus scheme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">€5.000,- dedicated budget every 3 years for professional development</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commuting travel reimbursement + Lease a Bike plan</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An office in the city centre of Amsterdam (Nieuwmarkt)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work where it feels best for you: we offer flexible (hybrid in-office) working arrangements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous employer pension contribution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid Volunteering Day</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to our electric company boat (also available for private use), free lunch, and lots of social activities – all part of the deal!</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Is this you?</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you ready to take the next step in your career with SkyNRG? Explore our vacancies and become part of our company of change makers. Together, we can change the future of flying.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For more information about SkyNRG visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.skynrg.com"><u>www.skynrg.com</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>📌 Please note: We do not accept sales inquiries or intermediary services.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At SkyNRG, we deeply value inclusion and diversity. As an equal opportunity employer, we are dedicated to ensuring every applicant has a fair chance, irrespective of race, color, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, or any other legally protected characteristics.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/skynrg/senior-business-development-lead-amsterdam-454312","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1793428830},{"slug":"shift-supervisor-dsl-01-delfzijl-101992","company_name":"Skynrg","title":"Shift Supervisor | DSL-01","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shift Supervisor | DSL-01</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Voor DSL-01 in Delfzijl zoeken wij een ervaren Shift Supervisor die vanaf de voorbereidingsfase meebouwt aan de operatie. Iemand die meedenkt over procedures, voorbereiding van de commissioning en startup en helpt om operators klaar te stomen voor het moment waarop de installatie daadwerkelijk gaat draaien. DSL-01 wordt een grootschalige productiefaciliteit voor Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF) en bijproducten.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Over de functie</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Als Shift Supervisor speel je een sleutelrol in de veilige, stabiele en efficiënte operatie van DSL-01. In deze functie krijg je een unieke combinatie van projectwerk en operationele verantwoordelijkheid. Tijdens de huidige projectfase draag je in dagdienst actief bij aan de voorbereiding van de fabrieksoperatie, commissioning en startup. Zodra DSL-01 operationeel is, gepland vanaf voorjaar 2028, geef je (in ploegendienst) leiding aan een ploeg operators en ben je verantwoordelijk voor de dagelijkse aansturing van een complexe chemische productie-installatie.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je zorgt ervoor dat productie-, kwaliteits-, veiligheids- en milieudoelstellingen worden behaald en neemt de leiding wanneer zich afwijkingen, storingen of noodsituaties voordoen. Daarbij werk je nauw samen met collega's van Maintenance, Engineering, Quality, Supply Chain en HSES.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wat deze rol bijzonder maakt, is dat je niet instapt in een bestaande organisatie, maar vanaf het begin meebouwt aan de operatie, productie en manier van werken.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Jouw verantwoordelijkheden</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tijdens de <strong>project- en opstartfase</strong> (~1,5 jaar):</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Werk je in dagdienst</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Draag je bij aan de commissioning en inbedrijfstelling van DSL-01</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ontwikkel je procedures en werkinstructies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Speel je een belangrijke rol in het uitvoeren van trainingsprogramma's en het trainen van operators</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ondersteun je bij de opbouw van de operationele organisatie</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Zorg je voor een succesvolle voorbereiding op de start van de fabriek.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">In de<strong> operationele fase </strong>(vanaf medio 2028):</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Geef je leiding aan een team van ongeveer 8 operators in een 5-ploegendienst binnen een volcontinu productieproces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bewaak je de veilige en efficiënte productie van SAF, propaan, butaan en nafta.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor je procesprestaties via DCS- en MES-systemen, stuur je bij waar nodig en zorg je ervoor dat productie-, kwaliteits- en rendementsdoelstellingen worden gerealiseerd.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Daarnaast ben je verantwoordelijk voor het naleven van veiligheids-, milieu- en kwaliteitsstandaarden, neem je de leiding bij incidenten en calamiteiten en coördineer je werkzaamheden tussen Operations, Maintenance en andere betrokken disciplines. Ook speel je een actieve rol in het continu verbeteren van processen en het verder versterken van de veiligheidscultuur binnen de fabriek.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een belangrijk onderdeel van je rol is het ontwikkelen van het operationele team. Je bent verantwoordelijk voor de groei van operators, zowel op technisch vlak als in competenties zoals samenwerking, eigenaarschap en veiligheidsbewustzijn. Door coaching, begeleiding en duidelijke verwachtingen zorg je voor een sterk team dat veilig, effectief en met vertrouwen kan opereren.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Jouw profiel</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">SkyNRG is een groeiende organisatie in een snel ontwikkelende markt. Daarom zoeken we mensen die zich prettig voelen in een omgeving waar nog niet alles vastligt en die actief willen bijdragen aan de verdere opbouw van de organisatie.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je neemt verantwoordelijkheid, denkt vooruit en voelt je op je plek in een omgeving die continu in beweging is.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je herkent jezelf in het volgende:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ervaring en affiniteit met Procestechniek, Chemische Technologie of een vergelijkbare richting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Minimaal een afgeronde VAPRO C of AOT niveau 4-opleiding</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Minimaal 10 jaar ervaring binnen de chemische, petrochemische, raffinage- of vergelijkbare procesindustrie</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aantoonbare operationele leidinggevende ervaring en bewezen people development skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ervaring met procesautomatisering en het werken met DCS- en MES-systemen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kennis van procesveiligheid, werkvergunningensystemen en relevante wet- en regelgeving</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ervaring met het nemen van operationele beslissingen in situaties waar veiligheid, kwaliteit en continuïteit samenkomen</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Welkome extra kennis en ervaring:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ervaring binnen greenfield-projecten of grootschalige industriële bouw- en opstartprojecten</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ervaring met commissioning, startup en operational readiness</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kennis van raffinage-, hydroprocessing- of duurzame brandstofprocessen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ervaring met continue verbeterprogramma's en performance management</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Over DSL-01</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In Delfzijl bouwen wij aan DSL-01, een fabriek van SkyNRG voor hernieuwbare brandstoffen. Hier produceren we Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF) uit reststromen zoals gebruikte vetten en oliën, met HEFA-technologie. Daarnaast maken we bijproducten zoals butaan, propaan en nafta.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">DSL-01 wordt de eerste fabriek in Europa die volledig gericht is op SAF en bijbehorende duurzame bijproducten. Als de fabriek in bedrijf is, produceren we jaarlijks 100.000 ton SAF en 35.000 ton bijproducten. Daarmee verminderen we de uitstoot van broeikasgassen met circa 80% ten opzichte van fossiele kerosine, gemeten over de hele keten.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">De bouw is gestart in 2026 en de eerste productie staat gepland voor 2028. Het project omvat de fabriek zelf, bijbehorende leidingen en tijdelijke werkterreinen. Je draagt direct bij aan de realisatie van een nieuwe industriële fabriek en de verduurzaming van de luchtvaart.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We werken volgens internationale standaarden en Nederlandse wet- en regelgeving om de impact op mens, natuur en omgeving zorgvuldig te beheersen. Veiligheid, duurzaamheid en samenwerking staan daarbij centraal.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Waarom deze rol?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deze functie biedt een kans die maar weinig operators en shift supervisors krijgen. Je bent vanaf een vroeg stadium betrokken bij de realisatie van een compleet nieuwe fabriek en kunt jouw operationele expertise inzetten om invloed uit te oefenen op commissioning, procedures, opleidingen en de uiteindelijke manier van werken.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Na de opstart maak je de stap naar een operationele omgeving waarin je leiding geeft aan een moderne productie-installatie en een belangrijke rol speelt in het neerzetten van de standaarden, cultuur en prestaties van de fabriek.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tegelijkertijd draag je direct bij aan de realisatie van een van Europa's eerste grootschalige SAF-fabrieken. Een unieke kans om mee te bouwen aan een nieuwe productieorganisatie én een tastbare bijdrage te leveren aan de verduurzaming van de luchtvaart.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>NB: Voor de opbouw van de operationele organisatie zoeken we uiteindelijk vijf Shift Supervisors. De eerste twee Supervisors starten tijdens de project- en opstartfase van DSL-01. De overige drie posities worden naar verwachting in het voorjaar ingevuld, zodat het volledige team gereed is voor de operationele fase. ‌</em></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Solliciteer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wil jij meewerken aan de succesvolle realisatie van een nieuwe fabriek en het resultaat van je werk terugzien in de praktijk? Dan is dit je kans om bij te dragen aan de ontwikkeling van duurzame luchtvaart.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>NB: Een medische keuring maakt vanwege veiligheids- en gezondheidsredenen onderdeel uit van de selectieprocedure voor deze functie. ‌</em></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meer weten over DSL-01 en SkyNRG? Kijk op <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.skynrg.com"><u>www.skynrg.com</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📌 Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>SkyNRG is een werkgever die gelijke kansen biedt. We zetten ons in voor een inclusieve werkomgeving en beoordelen alle sollicitanten op basis van hun kwaliteiten, ongeacht afkomst, huidskleur, religie, nationaliteit, geslacht, seksuele oriëntatie, genderidentiteit of -expressie, leeftijd, beperking of andere wettelijk beschermde kenmerken.</em></p><hr><p>Compensation: €4,583 – €6,000 per month</p><ul><li>Shift Supervisors, DSL-01 • Bruto maandsalaris, incl vakantiegeld €4,583 – €6,000 per month</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/skynrg/shift-supervisor-dsl-01-delfzijl-101992","tags":["DSL-01 Operate"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Delfzijl","created_at":1793428830},{"slug":"technical-program-manager-delft-125247","company_name":"Quantware","title":"Technical Program Manager","description":"<h2><strong>About Us </strong><br /></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">QuantWare is building the world’s most powerful quantum processors to solve humanity's greatest challenges. We do this with our unique VIO™ technology, the only QPU architecture that breaks the hardware barriers that have held quantum computing back, unlocking the path to MegaQubit quantum processors.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With VIO, we are paving the way for the hyper-scale quantum computers that will change the world. And delivering on that vision demands people who don’t shy away from tackling the hardest challenges of our time. That’s where you come in! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us as a <strong>Technical Program Manager</strong> in our new Project Management Office (PMO), reporting to the PMO Lead. You will own day-to-day program management for one to two development programs, keeping schedules, responsibilities and risks visible across development and production departments. Working in a highly technical, fast-moving environment, you will build the habits and practice of program discipline that the whole company will adopt as the PMO scales.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll be doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership and responsibility</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own top level execution and delivery of assigned programs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with project and discipline leads on cross-department programs to ensure execution on schedule and within budget.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the day-to-day execution of the assigned programs including handoffs across departments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the program-management activities for your assigned programs: schedule build, baselining, gate reviews, etc.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manage uncertainty and risk</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify risks and bottlenecks early</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan for potential failure modes and contingencies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Escalate risks and blockers to the relevant stakeholders promptly.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support growth and development of the team</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentor junior program managers in program execution and collaborative leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the PMO Lead in rolling out common language, product lifecycle, team rhythms for programs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support general program management training across the organization.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Profile</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leadership experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Over 6 years of experience, including more than 4 years managing the delivery of complex, research-intensive chip hardware projects in a program management role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead programs coordinating across functions and departments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to work with highly specialised technical experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in a fast-moving start-up or scale-up environment balancing hands-on technical leadership with growing a team, as a strong plus.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Approach</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn quickly in a highly technical, low-maturity field, without needing a deep technical background in quantum computing on day one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate a long-term strategy into an execution plan for your program teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical skills with the ability to make pragmatic, informed decisions under uncertainty.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring together world-class technical experts and project leads to execute on highly complex programs.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Background</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MSc, PhD, or equivalent experience in physics, electrical engineering, microwave/RF engineering, semiconductor technology, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of the development lifecycle for chip-level technologies; experience with superconducting qubits or cryogenic systems is a strong plus.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Communication</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communicator who can motivate teams, facilitate alignment, adept at communicating program management ideas to highly technical people.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with stakeholders and colleagues across the organization - Product, Research and Development, Operations, Management team, etc.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate fluently in English.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Don't tick every box? Apply anyway! Research shows women often self-select out if they don't meet every requirement. Here's our take: nobody ticks every box. This is a description of our ideal candidate, not a filter. If most resonates and you're keen to learn the gaps, apply. We hire for trajectory, not perfection. <br /><br /><strong>What We Offer:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At QuantWare, you’ll be part of a high-performing team of world-class experts in an ambitious, fast-moving environment. From day one, you’ll have the trust, tools, and support to do your best work. Here’s what you can expect:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive salary</strong> - A salary that reflects the impact and importance of the role (and of course 8% holiday allowance)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension that’s built to last</strong> - A generous and future-proof pension plan that includes partner and dependent coverage.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexibility built on trust</strong> - We focus on outcomes. Work flexibly, in a hybrid setup, with an open vacation policy that lets you manage your time</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Personal growth</strong> - We invest in your L&amp;D, with a budget available to each team member, dependent on their individual ambitions, development needs, and performance</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A connected team</strong> - We make space to celebrate wins together, with team events, offsites, and spontaneous moments that bring us closer<br /><br /><strong>Diversity &amp; Inclusion at QuantWare</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re an ambitious company, not only for our goals but also to become an even more diverse and inclusive team. We know great candidates don't always follow a straight path, and we value diverse experience, perspectives, and ways of thinking. We know this helps us make better decisions, drives more innovation, and strengthens our culture. <br /><br /><em>As part of our recruitment process, candidates may be required to undergo pre-employment screening.</em></p><h2></h2><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/quantware/technical-program-manager-delft-125247","tags":["Research & Development"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Delft","created_at":1793428830},{"slug":"embedded-engineer-eindhoven-135627","company_name":"Aim Solutions","title":"Embedded Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Eindhoven, the Netherlands (on-site, High Tech Campus) | <strong>Type:</strong> Full-time | <strong>Level:</strong> Medior–Senior, ~5 years of relevant experience</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AIM Solutions is an early-stage deep-tech startup in Eindhoven building inspection and metrology equipment for the semiconductor industry. We are in an active build phase: a small, growing team turning lab setups into a tool that does not exist anywhere else yet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Embedded Engineer you own everything between the instrument hardware and our acquisition software. You integrate cameras, frame grabbers, motion controllers, piezo stages, lasers and FPGA timing hardware, and you make them run as one synchronized, reliable scan. The work is hands-on: vendor SDKs, trigger wiring, PCIe cards and lab networks one day, clean driver code and a live data stream to the user interface the next. You work closely with the System, Mechatronics, Application and Algorithm engineers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design the trigger and acquisition architecture that synchronizes camera exposure, stage motion and laser pulses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integrate industrial cameras and frame grabbers through industry-standard interfaces and vendor SDKs, from driver set-up to stable high-rate acquisition.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integrate motion controllers and positioning stages through vendor APIs and controller scripting, including commissioning and tuning with the Mechatronics Engineer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and extend FPGA-based timing and I/O for triggering and position-synchronized acquisition.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write driver and control layers in C/C++ and Python that the scan and reconstruction software builds on, and expose live status and data streams to the user interface.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the instrument PC and lab network set-up: PCIe hardware, high-speed Ethernet links between devices, IP planning and device discovery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring up and debug hardware in the lab with oscilloscope, logic analyzer and network captures, and document interfaces and timing budgets with the System Engineer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take part in code review and help move the set-up from prototype to a reproducible, maintainable tool.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your profile</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MSc in Electrical Engineering, Embedded Systems, Applied Physics or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">~5 years of hands-on experience integrating and controlling hardware, preferably in high-tech equipment, scientific instruments or industrial automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong C/C++ and Python, including working with vendor SDKs and drivers on Windows and Linux.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience with hardware triggering and synchronization of multiple devices (cameras, motion, lasers, DAQ).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with FPGA development or working closely with FPGA-based timing hardware.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid grasp of hardware interfaces and networking: Ethernet, USB, serial, PCIe, and multi-device lab networks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable in the lab: reading schematics, using an oscilloscope and logic analyzer, and debugging where hardware and software meet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Git and collaborative code review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full professional proficiency in English.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value judgment and ownership over a perfect match. If you recognize yourself in most of this, we would like to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with machine-vision cameras, frame grabbers or high-throughput image acquisition.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with precision motion controllers and encoder-based position triggering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High-speed data paths to a host PC, SoC FPGAs or Linux driver development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building lightweight web or API layers for instrument control and live data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in optics, lasers, coherent imaging, semiconductor metrology or lithography equipment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with CI, hardware-in-the-loop testing, or working in a Scrum team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership of the embedded and timing backbone of a tool that does not exist anywhere else yet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A small team with short feedback loops and real impact on the product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on work at the meeting point of hardware, optics and software, on the High Tech Campus Eindhoven.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A competitive salary for the Dutch market.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/aim-solutions/embedded-engineer-eindhoven-135627","tags":["Development & Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Headquarter","created_at":1793428830},{"slug":"senior-lead-lifecycle-marketing-manager-full-remote-netherlands-96246","company_name":"EverAI","title":"Senior/Lead Lifecycle Marketing Manager (Full Remote - Netherlands)","description":"<h1>Our Vision &amp; Products</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>🚀 EverAI — Building the Future of AI Companionship</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>One of the Top 15 Largest &amp; Fastest-Growing AI Companies in the World</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>50 Million Users in 2 years — Help Us Reach 100M first, 500M next</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At <strong>EverAI</strong>, we’re shaping what it means to connect with AI. With <strong>50 million users and counting</strong>, we're not just building products — we're creating entirely new categories.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our flagship product is the <strong>world’s largest AI companionship platform</strong>, redefining relationships for millions. It is governed by our proprietary moderation system, EverGuard — an internal AI designed to ensure everything we build is <strong>safe, ethical, and human-first</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>And we’re only just getting started!</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Our Team</h1><p style