ing, retention, reactivation, and LTV through smarter segmentation, personalization, and timing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Test big ideas quickly:</strong> build experiments, measure what genuinely moved the numbers, scale the winners, and turn each result into the next opportunity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make ambitious CRM ideas possible:</strong> work directly with Product, Data, Engineering, and Creative to improve the tooling, tracking, messages, offers, and reporting behind the channel</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Your Qualifications</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’ve scaled CRM before:</strong> you can show significant improvements you personally drove in revenue, conversion, repeat purchases, retention, reactivation, or LTV, with real numbers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You understand consumer growth:</strong> you’ve worked in a high-volume B2C subscription business, where CRM had a direct effect on revenue</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You think like a builder:</strong> you do not stop at recommendations; you can personally create segments, journeys, experiments, campaign logic, and performance analysis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You know how to find and prove what works:</strong> you can turn user behavior into ideas and use testing, control groups, attribution, and incrementality to validate the results</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You move quickly and take ownership:</strong> you are comfortable building without a finished playbook, deciding what matters most, and creating momentum without waiting for perfect information</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You communicate clearly and work across teams:</strong> you collaborate directly with technical, creative, and commercial stakeholders in English</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You are comf