xpertise; experience in building and maintaining customer relationships.</p></li><li><p>Fluent in Dutch and English.</p></li><li><p></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Your responsibilities will include:</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Managing organisational changes, from problem analysis, optimization of processes to designing and implementing new business models.</p></li><li><p>Developing different organisational transformation strategies and approaches (making an ambition strategy, design and guiding principles, organizational structure and required communication and engagement plans) that fits the client’s challenge best.</p></li><li><p>Managing and regulating Organisational Transformation projects, with high emphasis on both delivery as stakeholder management.</p></li><li><p>Building and maintaining a relevant network with current and new clients</p></li><li><p>Managing and guiding consultants during projects and in their personal development.</p></li><li><p>Co-develop one of the industries in which Valcon is present.</p></li><li><p>Building and promoting ‘Valcon’; focus on expanding the Business Change Capability, and primary Organisational Transformation.   </p></li></ul><h2><strong>What do we offer you?</strong></h2><ul><li><p><strong>Personal development:</strong> a tailor-made growth path with training, courses, certification and mentoring by experienced colleagues.</p></li><li><p><strong>An innovative work environment:</strong> collaborate with a team of experts pushing boundaries in data, technology, and consulting.</p></li><li><p><strong>Immediate impact and responsibility: </strong>you’ll make a difference for our clients from day one and are entrusted with responsibilities that challenge you to bring the best out of yourself.</p></li><li><p><strong>Inspiring work culture:</strong> a supportive, flexible, and no-nonsense environment that fosters your growth and fully allows you to be yourself.   </p></li></ul><p></p><h2><strong>Additionally, we offer:</strong></h2><ul>